## 6. Chrome Extension Webhook (Auto-Apply)
**Goal:** Highlight JD text on LinkedIn -> Click Extension -> Webhook -> Auto Generate PDF.

### Technical Implementation
1. **Chrome Extension (Vite/React):**
   - Create a `manifest.json` (V3).
   - Use `chrome.scripting.executeScript` to extract `document.body.innerText` from the LinkedIn Job posting.
   ```javascript
   // background.js
   chrome.action.onClicked.addListener(async (tab) => {
     chrome.scripting.executeScript({
       target: { tabId: tab.id },
       function: () => {
          const jdText = document.querySelector('.jobs-description__container').innerText;
          fetch('https://your-api.com/api/resumes/webhook/auto-generate', {
              method: "POST",
              headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json", "Authorization": "Bearer USER_TOKEN" },
              body: JSON.stringify({ job_description: jdText })
          });
       }
     });
   });
   ```
2. **Backend Webhook Endpoint:**
   - Build an endpoint taking raw text, mapping it to the default Resume Template for that user, and executing the LangGraph in a background task (`BackgroundTasks` in FastAPI), emailing the user the PDF when done.
